---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/role-page.css';
---
<Layout
  title="Cytidel for Analysts · Cytidel"
  description="Stop spending half your day stitching intelligence together from a dozen sources. Get back to the analysis only you can do."
>
  <div class="role-page">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h1">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Solution Guide</span>
          <h1 id="hero-h1">Cytidel for <span class="role">Analysts</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">Stop spending half your day stitching intelligence together from a dozen sources. Get back to the analysis only you can do.</p>
          <div class="hero-cta">
            <a href="/book-a-demo" class="btn btn-primary">
              Book a Demo
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pains" aria-labelledby="pains-h2">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="pains-h2">What's getting in your way</h2>
          <p class="lead">Three problems every security analyst is wrestling with day to day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pain-grid">
          <article class="pain">
            <span class="pain-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h10"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Half your day is correlation work.</h3>
            <p>Pulling CVE data from scanners. Cross-referencing against threat feeds. Checking exploit repos. Searching for vendor advisories. Building the same spreadsheet you built last week. The work is necessary, repetitive, and not what you trained for.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pain">
            <span class="pain-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3v18h18"/><path d="M7 14l3-3 3 3 4-5"/></svg></span>
            <h3>You're researching the wrong things.</h3>
            <p>Trending vulnerabilities make noise; not all of them affect your stack. By the time you've worked out which ones do, the actual high-priority items have been waiting hours for your attention.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pain">
            <span class="pain-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l8 3v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 10-4.5-2-8-5-8-10V6z"/></svg></span>
            <h3>Your team can't keep up, and the volume keeps growing.</h3>
            <p>The workload doubles every two years. Your team hasn't. You're not slow — you're stretched thin across work that no human-scale team can sustainably do manually.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="cap-h2">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="cap-h2">What Cytidel does for analysts</h2>
          <p class="lead">Cytidel automates the correlation work, so your time goes to the work that actually needs a human.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="capabilities-list">
          <div class="cap-item">
            <span class="cap-no">01</span>
            <div><h3>Real-time Vulnerability Intelligence</h3><p>tags and rates every vulnerability automatically. Exploitation status, threat actor association, exploit availability — all surfaced, all updated continuously, all backed by an evidence trail you can read in seconds.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-item">
            <span class="cap-no">02</span>
            <div><h3>Bulk Analyser</h3><p>processes your scanner output in minutes. Upload, see what's genuinely dangerous, see what's noise, save the report. The manual cross-referencing work is done.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-item">
            <span class="cap-no">03</span>
            <div><h3>Smart Alerts</h3><p>brings the right signal to you. When something relevant to your stack appears across thousands of sources, you hear about it — without having to monitor everything.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-item">
            <span class="cap-no">04</span>
            <div><h3>Threat Actor Intelligence</h3><p>gives you adversary context without the research project. Every actor mapped to their vulnerabilities, TTPs, and campaign history. You spend your analytical time on the deeper questions, not on the basics.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="scenarios" aria-labelledby="scen-h2">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="scenario-card">
          <div class="section-head">
            <h2 id="scen-h2">How analysts use Cytidel</h2>
            <p class="lead">Three moments where the work changes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-list">
            <article class="scenario">
              <div class="scenario-num">01</div>
              <div>
                <h3>Monday morning research, automated</h3>
                <p>You used to spend the first two hours every Monday rebuilding the picture — what's trending, what's exploited, what's relevant to your environment. Cytidel has it ready. You spend Monday morning on actual analysis, not research collection.</p>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="scenario">
              <div class="scenario-num">02</div>
              <div>
                <h3>The "are we vulnerable?" question, answered fast</h3>
                <p>A new CVE makes the news. Leadership wants to know if you're exposed. You check Cytidel against your stack and reply with a structured answer in minutes — exploitation status, threat actor association, your environment's exposure. Not a half-day research task.</p>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="scenario">
              <div class="scenario-num">03</div>
              <div>
                <h3>The deeper work you actually want to do</h3>
                <p>With the correlation work automated, your time goes to the analysis that needs a human — campaign patterns, attribution work, the questions that don't have a feed. You become more valuable, not just faster.</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="conversation" aria-labelledby="conv-h2">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="conv-h2">The conversation it changes</h2>
          <p class="lead">You stop being a search engine. You start being an analyst.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="conversation-grid">
          <div class="conv">
            <span class="conv-label">The old conversation</span>
            <p>"Did you look into that CVE that came out yesterday?" / "I'm getting to it. I'm still working through last week's queue."</p>
            <div class="conv-verdict"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M15 9l-6 6M9 9l6 6"/></svg>Time lost to work that should be automatic.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="conv is-new">
            <span class="conv-label">The new conversation</span>
            <p>"That CVE's already mapped to APT28 in Cytidel. I'm looking at the campaign-level pattern — there's something interesting about how they're chaining it with last month's vulnerability."</p>
            <div class="conv-verdict"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-6"/></svg>Doing the work you were hired to do.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="final-cta-h2">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="final-cta-card">
          <h2 id="final-cta-h2">Ready to see Cytidel?</h2>
          <p>Meet with a Cytidel expert to discuss how you can get ahead of emerging threats, understand the latest threat actor activity relevant to your business, and monitor critical software and suppliers 24/7.</p>
          <a href="/book-a-demo" class="btn btn-primary">
            Book a Demo
            <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
